\fs96 \cf2 System requirements\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa400\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 You can install Mojo on any Mac, Linux, or Windows (with WSL) system that meets the requirements below.\
For installation instructions, see the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/manual/install/"}}{\fldrslt \cf5 \ul \ulc5 install guide}}.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Mac\cf6 LinuxWindows\cf2 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
macOS Sequoia (15) or later\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Apple silicon (M1 - M5 processor)\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Python 3.10 - 3.14\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Xcode or Xcode Command Line Tools 16 or later\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
We have \cf5 \ul \ulc5 limited compatibility\cf2 \ulnone  for Apple Silicon GPUs. You may need to run 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 xcodebuild -downloadComponent MetalToolchain
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 , which downloads the Metal utilities required for GPU programming in later versions of Xcode.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa800\partightenfactor0

\fs64 \cf2 GPU compatibility\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 Mojo supports both CPUs and GPUs, so you don't need a GPU to program with Mojo. But if you do want to program for GPUs with Mojo, keep reading to make sure your GPU is compatible with Mojo.\
Because we don't test every variant of a GPU architecture, we've divided our list of compatible GPUs into 3 tiers:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs48 \cf2 Tier 1: Fully supported\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 We provide full support and testing for the following data center GPUs:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
NVIDIA B200 (Blackwell)\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
NVIDIA H100 and H200 (Hopper)\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
AMD Instinct MI355X (CDNA4)\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
AMD Instinct MI300X and MI325X (CDNA3)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs48 \cf2 Tier 2: Confirmed compatibility\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 We've confirmed full compatibility with the following GPUs but we don't maintain tests for them:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls7\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
NVIDIA A100 and A10 (Ampere)\
\ls7\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
NVIDIA L4 and L40 (Ada Lovelace)\
\ls7\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
NVIDIA RTX 50XX series (Blackwell)\
\ls7\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
NVIDIA RTX 40XX series (Ada Lovelace)\
\ls7\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
NVIDIA RTX 30XX series (Ampere)\
\ls7\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
NVIDIA Jetson Orin and Orin Nano (Ampere)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs48 \cf2 Tier 3: Limited compatibility\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 We've either confirmed or received reports that the following GPUs work for GPU programming with Mojo. Some can also execute basic graphs with MAX APIs. However, none of these currently run major GenAI models with MAX:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls8\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Apple silicon GPUs (M1 - M5)\
\ls8\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
NVIDIA RTX 20XX series (Turing)\
\ls8\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
NVIDIA T4 (Turing)\
\ls8\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
AMD Radeon RX 9000 series (RDNA4)\
\ls8\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
AMD Radeon 800M series (RDNA3.5)\
\ls8\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
AMD Radeon 8050S / 8060S (RDNA3.5)\
\ls8\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
AMD Radeon 700M series (RDNA3)\
\ls8\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
AMD Radeon RX 7000 series (RDNA3)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs48 \cf2 Pre-Turing NVIDIA GPUs\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 Pre-Turing NVIDIA GPUs (such as Pascal-generation GTX 10XX and Tesla P100) are not supported out of the box. To use Mojo and MAX on these GPUs, set the 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 MODULAR_NVPTX_COMPILER_PATH
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  environment variable to point to a system 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 ptxas
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  binary compatible with your hardware and driver version.\
If you've had success with any GPUs not listed here, please {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://discord.gg/modular"}}{\fldrslt \cf5 \ul let us know on Discord}}.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs48 \cf2 GPU software requirements\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 Make sure you have the corresponding GPU software:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls9\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
If you're on an NVIDIA GPU:\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls9\ilvl1\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
NVIDIA GPU driver version 580 or higher\
\pard\tx1660\tx2160\pardeftab720\li2160\fi-2160\partightenfactor0
\ls9\ilvl2\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9642 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Check your NVIDIA GPU driver version using {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://developer.nvidia.com/system-management-interface"}}{\fldrslt \cf5 \ul nvidia-smi}}\
\ls9\ilvl2\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9642 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
To update, see the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/drivers/"}}{\fldrslt \cf5 \ul NVIDIA driver docs}}\
\ls9\ilvl2\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9642 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
For older driver versions, you can set the 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 MODULAR_NVPTX_COMPILER_PATH
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  environment variable to point to a system 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 ptxas
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  binary to bypass this requirement\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls9\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
If you're on an AMD GPU:\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls9\ilvl1\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
AMD GPU driver version 6.3.3 or higher\
\pard\tx1660\tx2160\pardeftab720\li2160\fi-2160\partightenfactor0
\ls9\ilvl2\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9642 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
For datacenter GPUs (MI300X/MI325X), see the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://rocm.docs.amd.com/projects/install-on-linux/en/latest/install/install-methods/package-manager/package-manager-ubuntu.html"}}{\fldrslt \cf5 \ul Ubuntu native install guide}}\
